prompt read REMEMBER + the three itinerary docs, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; Rye prioritized, Glow on green-witnessed Rye; approve own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates
think The living edge is Season G (Cryptography) — SHA-256 landed last commit, the suite GREEN across twenty-four files. Lindy-first, crux-first: the highest-Lindy new rung stands directly on that fresh SHA-256, and it is the keyed hash the deployed world reaches for first — HMAC-SHA-256 (TLS 1.3 PRF, JWT HS256, TOTP, the Signal/Bitcoin HKDF). It also unblocks a future HKDF-SHA-256 the way hmac_sha512 unblocked hkdf_sha512. Agent-doable, witness-provable, no custody crossed.
think Authored crypto/hmac_sha256.rye as the 256-bit sibling of the GREEN crypto/hmac_sha512.rye — same RFC 2104 / FIPS 198-1 construction, shapes inherited from sha256 (32-byte tag, 64-byte block), the key brought to block width (hashed first when longer), inner pass over (K0 XOR 0x36) ‖ msg, outer pass over (K0 XOR 0x5c) ‖ inner-digest. No new hashing — it composes the already-GREEN SHA-256, calling no std.crypto in the primitive.
think Parity proven at selftest against two references runnable now: the RFC 4231 Test Case 2 known-answer (key "Jefe", "what do ya want for nothing?" → 5bdcc146...ec3843) hex for hex, and Zig's independent std.crypto HmacSha256 byte-for-byte across a short key, a block-length key, a key longer than the block (the hash-the-key path), the empty message, and a multi-block message. Over-long message refuses MessageTooLong and over-long key refuses KeyTooLong before a byte is mixed.
obs GREEN on the first metal pass; tame_style_check bans clean (bare assert, no @memcpy, snake_case). Registered after hmac_sha512 in crypto_suite_witness.rish — whole-suite GREEN across all twenty-five files (twenty-two primitives + three compositions), exit 0.
